1: # Plan 6C: prepared boundary-aware smooth
2: 
3: Draft for independent mesh-hook and grid/acceptance adversarial reviews.
4: This bounded engine slice enables the actual BSMOOTH command used by SculptCore,
5: including main-plus-smooth programs with independently evaluated radius/stacks.
6: It does not claim general attribute, cavity, unbounded, dyntopo or host-stage support.
7: 
8: ## Implementation
9: 
10: 1. Add explicit hook metadata for a prepared-safe, scalar-independent pre-freeze
11:    phase and for the equivalent phase being unnecessary on grids. Only the
12:    boundary-class refresh is currently classified this way. Do not infer safety
13:    from callback pointer identity or permit ENHANCE/FEATURE_ALIGN/POLYGROUP hooks.
14:    Existing raw hook behavior is unchanged.
15: 2. Replace the blanket prepared attribute rejection with a narrow metadata check:
16:    read-only vertex INT bound to `.boundary.vert.class`, with no retargeting/use
17:    category or attribute overrides. Reject all other attribute bindings and every
18:    write. Mesh binding continues through existing exec; grids require the existing
19:    DefaultColumn routing and its documented zero/interior semantics. Keep every
20:    other capability guard, including attribute mirrors and active layer restrictions.
21: 3. Mesh prepared single/program entrypoints validate every command/scalar/radius
22:    before any hook/materialization/mutation. For an accepted nonempty region,
23:    run the classified pre-freeze hook before deciding topology freeze/thaw, and
24:    before any program geometry stage. Calling the boundary refresh on each
25:    accepted region is safe: it internally returns immediately unless boundaryDirty.
26:    This also handles an earlier empty dab without incorrectly skipping the first
27:    actual boundary refresh. Run at most once per identical invariant hook within
28:    that program; do not broaden raw runProgramHooks or deduplicate command-dependent
29:    hooks. Preserve each prepared stage's working scalar scope and common node union.
30: 4. Grid prepared execution binds the existing zero read-only column through
31:    execStage, after complete preflight. It runs no mesh-only hook. No new authored
32:    grid channels or attribute mirrors are created for the read-only boundary class.
33: 
34: ## Gate
35: 
36: - Multi-leaf mesh: compare prepared BSMOOTH and DRAW+BSMOOTH against independently
37:   evaluated wide-region raw references, including marked sharp/seam boundaries,
38:   live-disk and CSR neighbor modes, larger dynamic secondary radius, explicit
39:   empty vs inherited strength, varying inputs and projection values.
40: - Exact undo/redo and authored/working scalar restoration. Verify read-only
41:   boundary attributes are not overwritten by prepared stage values.
42: - Dirty boundary state with initially frozen topology and an earlier zero/miss
43:   dab: first actual smooth refresh must happen safely before freeze; no dropped
44:   topology pages are accessed. Failed later-command preflight leaves boundary
45:   dirty state, attribute inventory, geometry, logs and first-dab state unchanged.
46: - Multi-leaf grids: prepared BSMOOTH/program vs existing raw BSMOOTH references,
47:   immediate/deferred normals, independent stacks/radii, undo/redo and no added
48:   authored channels/mirrors. Zero class is intentionally the existing grid policy,
49:   not a claim of cage-boundary preservation parity with mesh BSMOOTH.
50: - Keep unsupported attribute/hook tests rejecting, including ENHANCE,
51:   FEATURE_ALIGN, POLYGROUP, wrong-type/domain/written attributes and overrides.
52: - Build native and Python via dispatcher, regenerate declarations if affected,
53:   run applicable native suites and exact-DLL Python/batch tests, stage package,
54:   then run the existing headed modal matrix plus actual autosmooth coverage.
55:   Record this bounded gate; remaining Plan 6 capabilities/consumers stay open.
